    "distinct_from_closed_families": [
      "The closed VIX risk-state family used an absolute VIX level transformed into a trailing percentile; this family uses only the same-date ratio of 30-day to three-month Cboe implied volatility and has no level percentile or lookback.",
      "The closed BTC realized-volatility term-structure family used BTC return variance at multiple horizons; this family contains no BTC-derived volatility feature.",
      "The closed VIX volatility-of-volatility, SKEW and volatility-target families used different external levels or continuous sizing; this family is one binary BTC-or-cash state based on the VIX/VIX3M relation.",
      "The open post-shock volatility family conditions on a three-percent BTC event and awaits forward evidence; this policy does not inspect BTC shock labels."
    ],
    "excluded_reinterpretations": [
      "No inverse relation, alternate ratio, smoothing, lookback, threshold, VIX or VIX3M absolute level, BTC interaction, fractional sizing, leverage or short leg may be added after outcome access.",
